# The production LNI is the sole activity-ingress boundary. Pre-create its
# canonical parent as mode 0750, owned by the layerxd uid and the configured
# client gid. The client has traverse/read access but cannot rename or unlink
# entries. The socket is created mode 0660, owned by layerxd and that client
# gid; SO_PEERCRED additionally requires the exact configured client uid/gid.
# The client uid MUST differ from the layerxd uid. Startup safely removes an
# owned stale socket after a crash, but refuses a live listener, foreign owner,
# non-socket entry, mutable parent or replaced path/inode. A persistent
# .layerxd-lni.lock regular file is pinned mode 0600 to the layerxd uid and held
# with an exclusive nonblocking advisory lock from before stale inspection
# through socket cleanup. Operators must not remove or replace that lock file.
# The layerxd service account must have the client gid as a supplementary group
# so it can assign that group to the newly bound socket.
LAYERX_NODE_LNI_SOCKET=/run/layerx/layerxd.lni.sock
LAYERX_NODE_LNI_ALLOWED_UID=1001
LAYERX_NODE_LNI_ALLOWED_GID=1001
LAYERX_NODE_CHECKPOINT_DIRECTORY=/var/lib/layerx/checkpoints

# Both values are mandatory and finite. Frame bytes include the LNI envelope
# and maximum finality registration evidence but exclude the four-byte
# transport prefix. The canonical value is fixed; a lower configured value is
# refused at startup rather than silently narrowing valid evidence bytes.
LAYERX_NODE_LNI_FRAME_BYTES=1146902
LAYERX_NODE_LNI_DEADLINE_MS=2000

# LAYERX_NODE_ACTIVITY_FIFO is intentionally unsupported. Operators grant the
# agent process access to the LNI socket rather than exposing a second ingress.

# LNI 1.3 advertises authenticated_durable_submit. For every SubmitRequest,
# layerxd verifies the canonical signature and the signing key against the
# current identity state before it acquires queue capacity. SubmitResponse is
# written only after the activity and assigned global sequence are appended to
# the owner-only admission journal in LAYERX_NODE_CHECKPOINT_DIRECTORY and
# fdatasync succeeds. That directory must reside on durable local storage (not
# tmpfs, /run, or an ephemeral container layer), be owned by the layerxd uid,
# and deny group/other writes. The socket directory and persistent admission
# directory must be distinct.
# Startup replays the journal only beyond the completed Programs feed frontier;
# the independent batch/WAL path verifies the signature again. ErrorResponse
# refusal class 6 carries the typed authentication result, never changes queue
# occupancy, and increments the SO_PEERCRED pid/uid/gid plus connection-
# generation counter exposed by lxp_daemon_lni_observability_snapshot.
